  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><strong>Freidel-Crafts Acylation:</strong></p><ul> <li>Friedel-Crafts acylation reaction is a type of reaction where an acyl group is added to an aromatic ring.</li> <li>This reaction occurs in the presence of an acid chloride <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math> and a Lewis acid catalyst like Aluminium chloride <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.</li> <li>Friedel-Crafts acylation reaction, changes the aromatic ring into a aromatic ketone.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/de8f3d55-e97a-44e6-8539-3bf23280d899.png\" style=\"width: 704px; height: 521px;\"/></li></ul>",
    "image": null
  },
